{"case_id": "MB_17", "timestep": 3, "case_summary": "A 57-year-old man presents to the emergency department with several days of malaise, weakness, and night sweats. Today, he experienced a headache with blurry vision, thus prompting his presentation. The patient has a history of diabetes and is followed closely by an endocrinologist. Otherwise, he has lost 10 pounds over the past month. His temperature is 100°F (37.8°C), blood pressure is 122/90 mmHg, pulse is 84/min, respirations are 16/min, and oxygen saturation is 99% on room air. Physical exam is notable for a thin man but is otherwise unremarkable. His visual acuity is 20/100 in both eyes, though he says that he normally has 20/20 vision. His gait is mildly ataxic as well, but his neurological exam is otherwise nonfocal. Laboratory studies are ordered as seen below.\n\nHemoglobin: 10 g/dL\nHematocrit: 31%\nLeukocyte count: 57,500/mm^3 with 35% blasts\nPlatelet count: 109,000/mm^3\n\nSerum:\nNa+: 139 mEq/L\nCl-: 100 mEq/L\nK+: 4.1 Eq/L\nHCO3-: 22 mEq/L\nBUN: 20 mg/dL\nGlucose: 99 mg/dL\nCreatinine: 1.1 mg/dL\nCalcium: 10.0 mEq/L\n\nWhich of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nOptions:\nA. Acute lymphoblastic leukemia\nB. Acute myelogenous leukemia\nC. Chronic lymphocytic leukemia\nD. Chronic myelogenous leukemia\nE. Multiple myeloma\n", "root": {"label": "Subacute Systemic Constitutional Syndrome with Pancytopenia and Leukocytic Blasts of Uncertain Aetiology", "time_course": "subacute", "severity": "unspecified", "confidence": 0.7, "supporting_facts": ["Systemic constitutional features (malaise, weight loss, fever, night sweats)", "Pancytopenia (hemoglobin 10 g/dL, platelet count 109,000/mm³)", "Leukocytosis with blasts (35% blasts in a total of 57,500/mm³)", "History of diabetes (potential metabolic context)", "Uncharacterised neurological findings (atypical visual acuity, mild ataxia)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Infectious aetiology: less likely given pancytopenia with blasts rather than isolated neutrophilia", "Lymphoma: possible but less likely than acute leukemia given the presence of circulating blasts", "Myelodysplastic syndrome: could explain cytopenias but typically has lower blast percentages", "Multiple myeloma: seen in evidence phenotypes but lacks monoclonal protein confirmation", "Myeloproliferative disorder: seen in evidence phenotypes but requires specific lineage markers"], "alarm_features": ["Systemic constitutional symptoms (weight loss, fever, night sweats)", "Pancytopenia with leukocytosis and blasts", "Sudden visual acuity decline in a patient with normal baseline vision"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.10076288360640837, "posterior": 0.10076288360640837, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.057616683836036395, "posterior": 0.057616683836036395, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT