"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of lymphoid lineage markers (no lymphocytosis, no atypical lymphocytes) in lab findings disfavor de novo ALL?", "summary": "Lack of lymphoid markers weakly contradicts de novo ALL (B2.1), as ALL typically presents with lymphocytosis or atypical lymphocytes."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the lack of lymphoid lineage markers (no lymphocytosis, no CD3/CD7 positivity) in lab findings disfavor lymphoblastic lymphoma?", "summary": "Absence of CD3/CD7 positivity weakly argues against lymphoblastic lymphoma (B2.2), as these markers are expected in lymphoid lineage tumors."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of chronic lymphocytic leukemia features (lymphocytosis, monoclonal B-cells) in lab findings disfavor a diagnosis of CLL with transformation?", "summary": "Absence of chronic CLL features (e.g., lymphocytosis) moderately contradicts CLL with transformation (B2.3), as these are hallmark findings in such cases."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "What evidence is MOST INCONSISTENT with Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm? Identify the single strongest finding that argues against this diagnosis.", "summary": "The 35% blasts and pancytopenia provide the strongest evidence against CML in blast crisis (B3), though CML blast crisis can present similarly without splenomegaly."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B3", 0.647], ["B4", 0.113], ["B2", 0.082]]}, {"top": [["B3", 0.576], ["B3.1", 0.325], ["B3.2", 0.139]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No universal instability markers (airway compromise, severe respiratory failure, shock, or major neurological deterioration). Vital signs are stable with no immediate life-threatening findings.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B3.1: CML in blast crisis) has posteri